  "term": "releaser",
  "definition": "In historical psychological laboratory apparatus, a releaser was the part of reaction-time equipment that delivered or exposed the stimulus. It was arranged so that, at the moment the stimulus appeared or was applied, it also started the timing circuit for measuring the subject’s reaction.",
